# 🔴 THE FAILURE THIS PREVENTS, measured 2026-09-05 on a real Windows install.
# Git on Windows converts line endings on checkout by default, so every shell
# script arrived with CRLF and bash could not read them:
#
#     /usr/bin/env: 'bash\r': No such file or directory
#
# ⛔ ALL THREE GATES WERE DEAD — and `git` read the failing hook as exit 0, so a
# commit that should have been refused went through. ⚠️ A gate that dies quietly
# is worse than no gate: the person believes they are protected.

# ⭐ NOTHING IS CONVERTED. Not the scripts, not the documents, not the
# templates. What is committed is what lands on disk, on every platform.
#
# 🔴 MEASURED THE SAME DAY, and it is why this is one line instead of a list:
# marking documents as `text` told git to convert THEM — so a freshly cloned
# tree on Windows reported 19 files as modified that nobody had touched, and
# `check-clear-ready` refused the cut over changes that did not exist. ⛔ A repo
# that is dirty the moment it is cloned teaches people to ignore that warning.
#
# ⚠️ The engine reads every file with an explicit encoding and splits on "\n",
# so a document with CRLF costs nothing. A script with CRLF costs everything.
* -text
